# Hash-pinned engine binaries and data files must keep their EXACT bytes on
# every checkout (no CRLF/LF conversion), or their pinned SHA256 in the strategy
# / profile / trust-manifest JSONs will not match and the engine refuses to run.
#
# The whole engine tree is covered, not just bin/ and files/. The strategy JSONs
# are hash-pinned in trusted-manifest.json too, and listing only some of the
# pinned paths here is what shipped a dead v0.5.0 build: fortnite.json was stored
# with LF, a Windows runner checked it out as CRLF, its hash stopped matching,
# and EngineIntegrity.VerifyOrThrow refused to start the engine at all.
Engine/winws2/** -text
